    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "For the rider: the 5.00 SGD cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-05055 is refunded in full. POL-NS-24 lets a rider cancel at no charge when the driver has not reached the pickup by the scheduled pickup time plus five minutes, and the whole fee is then refunded. Your pickup was scheduled for 07:30 (trip record EV-TRIP-05055), so the deadline was 07:35, and that record reports arrived_by_deadline false with arrived_at null. The driver-device GPS trace EV-GPS-05055 (weight 1.0; 50 fixes, 100% coverage, no gap over 30 s) never places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius (arrival check corroborated false, nearest_fix null) and shows him stopped roughly 1.1 km from the pickup from 07:33:10 through your 07:37:40 cancellation, matching your account that he was still more than 1 km away. The missed deadline is therefore established, and the fare ledger EV-FARE-05055 (total_charged 5.00) is corrected by returning that 5.00. Because the fee is voided, POL-NS-21's free wait never matured - arrived_at is null, so the 300 s wait could not begin - and POL-NS-22, which fixes the 5.00 SGD figure only where the driver cancels after the free wait, does not authorise a charge where the rider cancelled and the driver never arrived.\n\nFor the driver: I accept your contact defence. You messaged at 07:31:10 and placed an answered 40-second in-app call at 07:33:20 (EV-TRIP-05055, EV-CHAT-05055), both before the 07:37:40 cancellation, so POL-NS-23 does not void the fee for lack of contact, and no 5.00 SGD goodwill credit under POL-NS-24 arises, because that credit applies only where you also failed to attempt contact. I have not escalated under POL-GEN-26: the fact POL-NS-24 turns on - whether you reached the pickup by 07:35 - is established by the record, and POL-NS-24 contains no exception for traffic. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-05055-01, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) leaves your congestion explanation unconfirmed, but a rule that does not turn on traffic cannot be changed by it, so no fact needed for this ruling is unestablishable. Nor does the amount matching the standard 5.00 SGD fee by itself make the charge lawful: the fee stands only where the no-show entitlement matured, and here it did not. Confidence rests on the trip record and the GPS trace, both at weight 1.0; the dispute value is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 band, so under POL-NS-26 this ruling is final."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
